    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d487">

                <pb facs="0849" n="779" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg779"/>

                <head>Mr. Hovey to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 100]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States, Lima,
                                Peru,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-11-14"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 14, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Since my last despatch, No. 98, dated 28th
                    ultimo, several unimportant outbreaks, in favor of the rebellion, have occurred
                    in different portions of the republic.</p>
                <p>As yet, Colonel Prado has not succeeded in conveying his siege trains to the camp
                    of his army, one league from Arequipa. The combat, about to commence near that
                    city, will, no doubt, be the decisive one, and my confidence still continues in
                    the success of the government arms.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with great respect, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ALVIN P. HOVEY.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
